        <item>
            <title>0.27.6</title>
            <pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:49:02 -0500</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>66</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.27.6</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>:root{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.45 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,system-ui,sans-serif;color:#1d1d1f;margin:0;padding:2px 4px}h3{font-size:13px;font-weight:600;margin:0 0 6px}ul{margin:0;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 4px}code{font:12px ui-monospace,Menlo,monospace}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){body{color:#f5f5f7}}</style><h3>What's new in Keeploop 0.27.6</h3><ul><li>A woken chat can open in iTerm or Warp instead of Terminal: pick the app under Settings &gt; Monitors &gt; When the chat is closed.</li><li>Agents with a route can watch every incoming call and voicemail (optionally missed calls only) and every new or changed note (optionally one folder).</li><li>Monitors on notifications, calls, notes, calendar and texts show their own fields in Settings &gt; Monitors and can be saved. Before, a notifications monitor (such as one watching Slack or Teams) could not be saved, and an edit could drop part of its filter.</li><li>Add to ChatGPT in Settings &gt; Remote access opens Keeploop in the ChatGPT plugin directory: choose Add there. With your own tunnel it still uses Create custom MCP server.</li><li>Codex delivery finds codex installed with nvm, so check_setup no longer says it cannot find the codex command.</li></ul>]]></description>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <enclosure url="https://github.com/keeploopapp/releases/releases/download/v0.27.6/Keeploop-0.27.6.dmg" length="45550781" type="application/octet-stream" sparkle:edSignature="eBXD7jzZIZe+MlDYyHkVk3Ofpj9PVKKHDBcemwd+Nl88pxZ0vJTY32JT3EqTrLzI6NbgfMVBPWA8dYbYKIoGDg=="/>
